# Production deploy targets

When the user says **push**, **deploy**, or **push and deploy**, use only these endpoints (see `PRODUCTION_URLS.md`):

| What | Canonical |
|------|-----------|
| Frontend | https://frontend-six-chi-37.vercel.app |
| API | https://wan-studio-api.onrender.com |
| Repo | https://github.com/wellswenger-svg/Maal (`main`) |

## Rules

- Do **not** create a new Vercel project or Render service for deploys.
- Deploy frontend to existing Vercel project `frontend` on team `wellswenger-1737s-projects` (alias `frontend-six-chi-37.vercel.app`).
- Deploy/redeploy API on existing Render service `wan-studio-api` (`srv-d9ot8spt0dsc73bqjv0g`).
- Keep `VITE_API_URL=https://wan-studio-api.onrender.com` and `CORS_ORIGINS=https://frontend-six-chi-37.vercel.app`.
- After restarting a Cloudflare tunnel, update Render `COMFYUI_URL` to the new tunnel URL and redeploy (or restart) the API.
- Never commit tokens from `tokens&cmd` or `.env`.
- For push/deploy auth, follow `.cursor/rules/tokens-and-auth.mdc` — read tokens from `tokens&cmd`, never browser GitHub login.
